# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime state — written by the app at runtime, never versioned
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every configuration created through the app — senders, HEC and syslog
# destinations, Assets & Identities, network pools, simulations — is persisted
# as a JSON file, and holds whatever HEC token, lab address or account name it
# was given.
#
# Ignoring the whole of log-generator/ catches a store added later without
# anyone naming it here. But that directory is not the only place they land:
# store_path() honours LOG_GENERATOR_STATE_DIR, and an earlier version resolved
# bare names against the working directory, so launching the app from the
# repository root wrote every store — tokens included — where nothing ignored
# them. Two HEC tokens reached a public repository exactly that way. So the
# stores are also named on their own, which matches them at any depth.
log-generator/*.json
log-generator/*.json.bak-*

senders_config.json
configurations.json
syslog_destinations.json
simulations_config.json
environment.json
network_pools.json
assets_identities.json

# Any backup taken before editing one of those.
*.bak-*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Splunk Technical Add-ons — reference material (39 MB), out of scope
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
TAs/

